.Dd 2026-10-28
.Dt yukitracker.conf 5
.Os Unix
.Sh NAME
.Nm yukitracker.conf
.Nd configuration file for yukitracker
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
configuration file specifies various options for configuring the behavior of the yukitracker program.
.Pp
Lines starting with '#' are comments and are ignored. Options are specified as 'keyword value' pairs.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width ".It access.proxy" -compact
.It listen.tcp_udp Ar address
Specifies an address yukitracker will listen on for both TCP and UDP connections. If none are specified, yukitracker listens on 0.0.0.0:6969 by default. Can be added more than once.
.Pp
.It listen.tcp Ar address
Specifies the address yukitracker will listen on for TCP connections. Can be added more than once.
.Pp
.It listen.udp Ar address
Specifies the address yukitracker will listen on for UDP connections. Can be added more than once.
.Pp
A listen statement may carry options after the address, as in
.Dl listen.udp 10.0.0.5:6969 workers=4 shared
where
.Cm workers Ns = Ns Ar count
sets the worker count for that socket alone and is ignored for TCP, and
.Cm shared
permits another process to bind the same address.
.Pp
.It listen.udp.workers Ar threads
Specifies how many threads will be spawned to handle UDP requests, for every
listen statement that does not carry a
.Cm workers
option of its own. Defaults to 1. A count of 0 serves UDP from the event loop,
in the thread that also serves TCP. See
.Sx TUNING
before raising it.
.Pp
.It listen.tcp.workers Ar threads
Specifies how many threads accept and answer HTTP connections, for every
listen statement that does not carry a
.Cm workers
option of its own. Defaults to 0, which serves them from the event loop. See
.Sx TUNING
before raising it.
.Pp
.It listen.shared Ar boolean
Permits another process to bind the same address, for every listen statement
that does not carry a
.Cm shared
option of its own. Defaults to 0, and is useful only where a second tracker is
deliberately run on the same address.
.Pp
.It access.whitelist Ar path/to/whitelist
Specifies the path to the whitelist file containing all torrent hashes that yukitracker will serve. Use this option if yukitracker runs in a non-open mode.
.Pp
.It access.blacklist Ar path/to/blacklist
Specifies the path to the blacklist file containing all torrent hashes that yukitracker will not serve. Use this option if yukitracker was compiled to allow blacklisting.
.Pp
.It access.fifo_add Ar path/to/adder.fifo
Specifies the path to the FIFO (named pipe) used for dynamic changesets to accesslists. Info hashes written to this FIFO will be added to the main accesslist file.
.Pp
.It access.fifo_delete Ar path/to/deleter.fifo
Specifies the path to the FIFO (named pipe) used for dynamic changesets to accesslists. Info hashes written to this FIFO will be removed from the main accesslist file.
.Pp
.It access.stats Ar ip_address_or_network
Specifies the IP address or network in CIDR notation allowed to fetch stats from yukitracker, in case they are restricted.
.Pp
.It access.stats_path Ar path
Specifies the path to the stats location. You can configure yukitracker to appear anywhere on your tracker. Defaults to /stats.
.Pp
.It access.proxy Ar ip_address_or_network
Specifies the IP address or network of the reverse proxies. YukiTracker will take the X-Forwarded-For address instead of the source IP address. Can be added more than once.
.Pp
.It access.fullscrape Ar ip_address_or_network
Specifies the IP address or network in CIDR notation allowed to fetch fullscrapes from yukitracker, in case they are restricted.
.Pp
.It livesync.cluster.listen Ar ip_address:port
Specifies the IP address and port yukitracker will listen on for incoming live
sync packets to keep a cluster of yukitrackers synchronized. Every member of a
cluster has to agree on the port, which is also the one packets are sent to.
.Pp
.It livesync.cluster.group Ar ip_address
Specifies the multicast group a cluster talks in. For reaosns of backwards
comaptibility with legacy trackers, it defaults to 224.0.23.5, which,
technically sits in a range IANA assigns on request.

A cluster of its own is better served by an address out of 239.192.0.0/14,
which RFC 2365 sets aside for private use. Packets carry a ttl of 1 either
way and never leave the local link. Must be a valid mulitcast address from
.Pa 224.0.0.0/4
.
.Pp
.It livesync.cluster.node_ip Ar ip_address
Specifies one trusted IP address for sync between trackers running in a cluster. Can be added more than once.
.Pp
.It tracker.rootdir Ar path
Specifies the directory yukitracker will chroot/chdir to. All black/white list files must be located in this directory.
.Pp
.It tracker.user Ar username
Specifies the user yukitracker will setuid to after binding to potentially privileged ports.
.Pp
.It tracker.redirect_url Ar URL
Specifies the URL yukitracker will redirect to in response to a "GET / HTTP" request.
.Pp
.It tracker.empty_torrent_timeout Ar minutes
Specifies how long a torrent that has no peers left in either family is held for
its download count alone.
Defaults to and is limited to 1440 minutes. Lower values save memory at the cost
of less realiable download counts. A value of zero immediately destroys empty
torrents.
.El
.Sh TUNING
A worker is a thread that blocks in a read until a datagram arrives. Where the
kernel spreads arriving datagrams over a group of sockets bound to one address,
yukitracker binds one socket per worker and throughput rises with the worker
count. Linux does so, and FreeBSD since 12.0. Where a kernel does not, every
worker reads the same socket and they contend for its receive queue, so more
than one worker costs throughput. yukitracker asks at start up and binds a
group only where the answer is yes.
.Pp
.Pp
A TCP worker accepts a connection and answers it on its own stack, without
the event loop seeing it at all; only a connection it cannot finish is handed
over. One worker serves less than none, because accepting leaves the event
loop's thread without anything gained in return, so the setting is worth
either 0 or at least 2.
.Pp
On FreeBSD the
.Xr accf_data 9
filter has the kernel hold a new connection until data arrives on it, so the
tracker is woken once with the request already there. yukitracker uses it
wherever it is available; enable it with
.Cm options ACCEPT_FILTER_DATA
in the kernel or
.Va kld_list Ns = Ns Qq accf_data
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
To specify the address yukitracker will listen on for both TCP and UDP connections:
.Dl listen.tcp_udp 0.0.0.0:6969
.Pp
To specify the address yukitracker will listen on for TCP connections:
.Dl listen.tcp 0.0.0.0
.Pp
To specify the address yukitracker will listen on for UDP connections:
.Dl listen.udp 0.0.0.0:6969
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr yukitracker 1
.Pp
.Sh YUKITRACKER CONFIGURATION
Use the supplied yukitracker.yaml for YAML keys and defaults. Validate with yukitracker -C -f yukitracker.yaml. This manual also describes the upstream text configuration.
